Z||000000||fiero56||04-23-2001||01:13 PM||||My '86 has done this ever since I bought it last year. <P>I bought my '86SE with both headlights up, with the owner telling me they didn't work right, and were unplugged. I opened the motors up, replaced the green bumpers since the previous owner had already replaced the gears. The problem is the passenger side motor won't shut off. It doesn't spin freely like stripped gears allow, but continues to attempt to spin once every second or two. One second the motor will take out the gear/linkage slack to go up, the next second it does it the opposite direction. I replaced the limit switch, didn't fix the problem. What is preventing the passenger circuit from opening once the limit switch is activated? Anyone have this problem before or know a possible culprit?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||04-23-2001||02:43 PM||||Drew, just a guess here but have you replaced the relay?? (located under the left front fender)||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||04-23-2001||09:28 PM||||Terry, I thought of that, but wondered why the drivers side didn't have the same problem. I'll check around the swap meet this weekend and see if I can find a handful of them(you never know whats good when its electrical).||||reg||1
